From 8baae160a467d09ce10079945b3cbcc5bc809abd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Albrecht Lohofener <albrechtloh@gmx.de>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 08:32:27 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] SNMP: fix tables with augments and index leaves from
 other tables

- snmp_table_getnext: reset the capacity of the column OID before
  parsing each column. yangext_oid_get() overwrites it with the parsed
  length, so a later, longer column OID (e.g. Q-BRIDGE-MIB's dot1qPvid
  augmenting BRIDGE-MIB's dot1dBasePortEntry) failed to parse and the
  request failed.
- GET and GETNEXT only return columns of the registered table entry:
  its OID plus one sub-identifier, and readable. An augmented list holds
  the columns of several entries; index leaves may be not-accessible or
  leafrefs to another table, whose OIDs they have (Q-BRIDGE-MIB's
  dot1qVlanStaticEntry). GET matched columns by OID length and last
  sub-identifier only, and returned such an index for another column.
- Scalars: translate an SMI default value like a value from the
  datastore, e.g. an enum name to its number, and use it only for
  configuration. MIBs translated by RFC 6643 are all state data, where a
  missing value does not exist; clixon_snmp returned the default.

Upstream-Status: Pending
